{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260506180143de1c43ea832e48e2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The only error is in RemindMeApp.swift. There are no errors from ContextEngine.swift itself. This is very strange - it means ContextEngine compiles fine but RemindMeApp can't find it.\n\nWait - this might be a concurrency issue. `RemindMeApp` is a struct (App protocol), and `ContextEngine` is `@MainActor`. When `ContextEngine` is `@MainActor`, accessing `ContextEngine.shared` from a non-async context in a closure might cause the \"cannot find\" error (which is how Swift sometimes reports actor isolation issues).\n\nThe `reminderProvider` closure is: `() -> (String, String)` - a synchronous closure. But `ContextEngine.shared.generate()` is now `@MainActor` isolated, so calling it from a non-isolated closure won't work.\n\nActually wait, `setupServices()` is called from `.onAppear` which runs on the main actor. And the closure is stored and called later. The issue is that the closure isn't `@MainActor`, so it can't call `@MainActor` methods.\n\nLet me check what `startPeriodicPush` expects for `reminderProvider`. It probably takes `() -> (String, String)`. Since `ContextEngine` is `@MainActor`, the call to `generate()` needs to be on the main actor.\n\nOptions:\n1. Remove `@MainActor` from ContextEngine and handle CalendarService access differently\n2. Make the closure `@MainActor`\n3. Use a non-isolated approach\n\nActually, the simplest fix is to not make ContextEngine `@MainActor`. The issue before was that it accesses `CalendarService.shared` which is `@MainActor`. But `CalendarService.shared` is a static property - accessing the reference to the singleton doesn't require MainActor. Calling methods on it does. But `generateCalendarReminders()` calls `fetchUpcomingEvents()` which calls `store.events(matching:)` which is thread-safe.\n\nActually, the original error \"cannot find 'ContextEngine' in scope\" happened BEFORE I added `@MainActor` too. Let me think again...\n\nWait, the FIRST build after creating ContextEngine succeeded. Then I modified RemindMeApp and ReminderFeedViewModel and it failed. So the change that broke it was the modification to RemindMeApp.swift.\n\nLet me re-read the modified RemindMeApp.swift to see what's going on.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33d24eb8-fca9-4f18-9721-28897c4bbc1b","uuid":"87fbf996-50a0-4743-9826-afb47b3a798b"}
